1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,132
I have been lying under my sheets for
three hours, frozen stiff in the dark.

2
00:00:06,152 --> 00:00:09,812
It is five thirty in the morning, and the
copper

3
00:00:09,832 --> 00:00:13,788
smell of blood in my bedroom is making me
gag.

4
00:00:13,808 --> 00:00:18,465
Across from my mattress, my parents are
staring straight at me.

5
00:00:18,485 --> 00:00:24,505
Their eyes never blink, and their mouths
hang wide open in the shadows.

6
00:00:24,525 --> 00:00:26,251
But they are not alive.

7
00:00:26,271 --> 00:00:28,303
Something dragged them here.

8
00:00:28,323 --> 00:00:32,767
And right now, that hairless thing is
crouched directly

9
00:00:32,787 --> 00:00:36,232
beneath my bed, waiting for me to move.

10
00:00:36,252 --> 00:00:38,024
Let us go back to the beginning.

11
00:00:38,624 --> 00:00:42,251
It all began around two thirty in the
morning.

12
00:00:42,271 --> 00:00:46,301
I was asleep in my room when a sharp,
jagged scream

13
00:00:46,321 --> 00:00:49,928
tore through the far end of the hallway.

14
00:00:49,948 --> 00:00:57,388
I woke up in a cold sweat, sitting upright
with my heart hammering against my ribs.

15
00:00:57,408 --> 00:01:01,130
The house immediately fell dead silent
again.

16
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:03,106
Not a floorboard creaked.

17
00:01:03,126 --> 00:01:10,326
I told myself it was just a bad dream, but
my stomach twisted with anxiety.

18
00:01:10,346 --> 00:01:16,415
Before going to check on my parents, I
realized I had to use the bathroom.

19
00:01:16,435 --> 00:01:23,383
Looking back now, taking that detour might
be the only reason I am still breathing.

20
00:01:23,403 --> 00:01:28,359
I slipped out of my sheets and crept down
the hallway on bare feet.

21
00:01:28,959 --> 00:01:31,138
The bathroom was pitch black.

22
00:01:31,158 --> 00:01:35,436
I did not dare turn on the overhead bulb,
only letting

23
00:01:35,456 --> 00:01:39,468
in the faint grey light from the high
window.

24
00:01:39,488 --> 00:01:45,680
When I stepped back into the doorway, I
felt a damp coldness against the carpet.

25
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:46,970
I looked down.

26
00:01:46,990 --> 00:01:52,344
Heavy, dark streaks trailed from the
master bedroom toward my door.

27
00:01:52,364 --> 00:01:54,849
Pure terror seized my throat.

28
00:01:54,869 --> 00:01:56,402
I did not scream.

29
00:01:56,422 --> 00:01:58,265
I did not investigate.

30
00:01:58,285 --> 00:02:03,506
Like a frightened child, I bolted back
into my room and dove

31
00:02:03,526 --> 00:02:08,411
under my blankets, pulling the fabric over
my eyes.

32
00:02:08,431 --> 00:02:14,415
I squeezed my eyelids shut and prayed that
the shadows were playing tricks on me.

33
00:02:14,435 --> 00:02:20,039
I told myself morning was coming, and that
dawn would wipe it all away.

34
00:02:20,639 --> 00:02:25,962
Then, in the dead silence of the bedroom,
my hinges began to groan.

35
00:02:25,982 --> 00:02:32,236
The door slowly swung inward, stopping
with a soft click against the frame.

36
00:02:32,256 --> 00:02:35,510
I dared to pull the blanket down just
enough

37
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:38,489
to expose one eye into the dim room.

38
00:02:38,509 --> 00:02:42,145
What stepped through the threshold was not
human.

39
00:02:42,165 --> 00:02:46,324
It was tall, hairless, and completely
naked, with

40
00:02:46,344 --> 00:02:50,697
pale leathery skin pulled tight over its
ribs.

41
00:02:50,717 --> 00:02:55,626
Its spine was bent in a heavy hunch, and
it possessed no

42
00:02:55,646 --> 00:03:00,856
eyes, only smooth, hollow sockets where
sight should be.

43
00:03:00,876 --> 00:03:04,707
Yet it moved with cold, calculating
purpose.

44
00:03:04,727 --> 00:03:10,507
In its long, sinewy arms, it was dragging
my mother and father

45
00:03:10,527 --> 00:03:15,298
across the floor, completely limp and
unresponsive.

46
00:03:15,898 --> 00:03:20,899
I had to bite my own tongue until it bled
to keep from screaming.

47
00:03:20,919 --> 00:03:23,739
The creature did not toss them aside.

48
00:03:23,759 --> 00:03:28,455
It began arranging them with sick,
methodical care.

49
00:03:28,475 --> 00:03:35,664
It hauled my father upright and propped
him against the side of my bed, turning

50
00:03:35,684 --> 00:03:41,954
his head so his blank, unblinking eyes
faced directly into mine.

51
00:03:41,974 --> 00:03:47,490
Then it dragged my mother to the desk
chair, seating her upright

52
00:03:47,510 --> 00:03:52,547
with her arms limp and her mouth gaping
open toward me.

53
00:03:52,567 --> 00:03:57,476
They looked like grotesque mannequins
staged for an audience.

54
00:03:57,496 --> 00:04:00,915
Next, the creature dipped its clawed
fingers

55
00:04:00,935 --> 00:04:04,420
into the dark fluid pooling on the floor.

56
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:10,303
It began dragging its hands across my
bedroom wall, painting thick,

57
00:04:10,323 --> 00:04:15,846
ritualistic symbols and a jagged circle
around the mirror.

58
00:04:15,866 --> 00:04:19,832
It was crafting what it considered its
masterpiece.

59
00:04:19,852 --> 00:04:25,744
At the center of the wall, it dragged its
nails into the plaster, carving

60
00:04:25,764 --> 00:04:30,704
a line of words that I could not yet read
in the pitch black.

61
00:04:31,304 --> 00:04:36,116
When it finished, the creature turned
slowly toward my mattress.

62
00:04:36,136 --> 00:04:42,605
I held my breath, relaxing my muscles and
pretending to be dead asleep.

63
00:04:42,625 --> 00:04:44,149
It did not strike.

64
00:04:44,169 --> 00:04:49,309
Instead, it sank down to all fours,
slithering beneath the

65
00:04:49,329 --> 00:04:54,502
frame of my bed like a spider retreating
into its hole.

66
00:04:54,522 --> 00:04:59,857
I felt the wooden slats beneath my spine
dip under its weight.

67
00:04:59,877 --> 00:05:01,767
That was three hours ago.

68
00:05:01,787 --> 00:05:05,557
Ever since, I have been trapped here,
watching

69
00:05:05,577 --> 00:05:09,647
the clock tick from two thirty to five
thirty.

70
00:05:09,667 --> 00:05:11,126
I cannot twitch.

71
00:05:11,146 --> 00:05:12,640
I cannot sneeze.

72
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:16,389
The second I show any sign of
consciousness, I know

73
00:05:16,409 --> 00:05:20,074
its claws will tear up through the
mattress.

74
00:05:20,094 --> 00:05:25,839
I considered throwing the sheets and
sprinting for the front door to

75
00:05:25,859 --> 00:05:31,285
scream for neighbors, but the creature is
inches below my heels.

76
00:05:31,885 --> 00:05:36,688
Over the past few hours, the sky outside
my window has

77
00:05:36,708 --> 00:05:41,722
turned from ink black to a pale, misty
pre-dawn grey.

78
00:05:41,742 --> 00:05:46,510
The faint light has begun washing across
the opposite wall.

79
00:05:46,530 --> 00:05:51,723
Against my will, my gaze drifted back to
the bloody inscription

80
00:05:51,743 --> 00:05:56,724
the creature had gouged into the plaster
above my desk.

81
00:05:56,744 --> 00:06:01,102
With my eyes fully adjusted to the morning
twilight,

82
00:06:01,122 --> 00:06:05,172
every single word became sharp and
legible.

83
00:06:05,192 --> 00:06:07,276
It was not a ritual chant.

84
00:06:07,296 --> 00:06:11,257
It was four simple words meant only for
me.

85
00:06:11,277 --> 00:06:13,899
It read: I know you are awake.

86
00:06:13,919 --> 00:06:17,999
This story was inspired by I Know You're
Awake,

87
00:06:18,019 --> 00:06:21,677
as published in creepypasta archives.

88
00:06:21,697 --> 00:06:22,906
Now tell me.

89
00:06:22,926 --> 00:06:24,674
Would you have looked under the bed?

